    "botanicals": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "eyebrow": {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "settings": {
            "text": "OVER TWO CENTURIES OF HERITAGE"
          }
        },
        "heading": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "A History of Distilling in Sutherland and the North Highlands",
            "size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The story of distilling on Sutherland Estates stretches back more than 200 years.&nbsp;</p><p>In 1819, the Marquess of Stafford, later the first Duke of Sutherland, established the original Clynelish Distillery in nearby Brora, just north of Golspie.</p><p>The distillery played an important role in the development of the local economy, providing a market for barley grown by local farmers and creating employment opportunities in East Sutherland.</p><p>This marked an important chapter in the history of distilling in the North Highlands, establishing a connection between the land, its people and the craft of spirit production.</p><p>Today, more than two centuries later, Lizzie and Boban are proud to continue that story through Dunrobin Highland Distillery.</p><p>While the spirit may be different, the inspiration remains closely connected to the same landscape, heritage and sense of place that have shaped Sutherland for generations.</p><p>From an idea sparked during a stag weekend to the creation of our very own Highland distillery, discover more about the journey that brought Dunrobin Gin to life.&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"/blogs/news/the-story-behind-dunrobin-highland-distillery-dunrobin-gin\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"The Story Behind Dunrobin Highland Distillery | Dunrobin Gin\">Read the full story behind Dunrobin Highland Distillery and Dunrobin.</a></p>"
          }
        },
