    "heritage": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "eyebrow": {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "settings": {
            "text": "NATURE AT THE HEART"
          }
        },
        "heading": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "Inspired by Golspie, Dunrobin Castle and the North Highland Landscape",
            "size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Every aspect of Dunrobin Highland Distillery has been inspired by its surroundings.&nbsp;</p><p>From the woodland and formal gardens of Dunrobin Castle to the rolling hills of Sutherland and the coastline overlooking the Moray Firth, the landscape of the North Highlands is woven into the story of Dunrobin Gin.</p><p>Our recipe was developed to capture something of this remarkable place, bringing together carefully selected botanicals that reflect the gardens, woodland and natural character of the Castle's surroundings.</p><p>Working closely with ethnobotanist&nbsp;<a href=\"https://susannemasters.com\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://susannemasters.com\">Susanne Masters</a>&nbsp;and Dunrobin Castle's Head Gardener, Iain Crisp, whose knowledge of the gardens and East Sutherland's growing conditions spans more than 20 years, we developed a distinctive Highland gin inspired by the landscape around us.</p><p>At its heart is a classic combination of juniper, coriander seed and angelica root, complemented by lemon, clove, rose-scented pelargonium and blackcurrant leaf.</p><p>The rose-scented pelargonium is carefully grown in the formal gardens of Dunrobin Castle, while the blackcurrant leaves are harvested from the Castle's kitchen gardens.</p><p>Together, these botanicals create a gin with a distinctive woodland character, combining earthy, piney and spiced notes with a delicate floral freshness.</p><p>A taste of Sutherland, inspired by the gardens, woodland and coastline of our Highland home.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
